From 193abb5945f235f3d8cfa197b41db828a61c8e99 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: u5 <u5@cohost-max>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 20:00:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] u5: 25-closure-size-gc: closures, lazy seqs and chunked seqs
 sized to what they hold; 256 MiB initial heap

- lazy_meta_ptr: meta out of line (null until set, atomic publish), for jit_closure,
  lazy_sequence, chunked_cons and integer_range (an inline lazy_meta is ~56 bytes)
- jit_closure: a pointer to an arity table codegen emits once per closure site (static)
  instead of 11 inline pointers; arity_flags in object's tail padding; 176 -> 40 bytes.
  jit_closure::create<Ctx> builds the box and its capture context in one GC block (fixed-arity
  closures; variadic unchanged). c_api's jank_closure_set_arity* write a private table copy.
- lazy_sequence: std::recursive_mutex (40 bytes) replaced by a recursive lock of a u32 owner
  token (in object's tail padding) and a u8 depth, taken only during first realization;
  144 -> 56 bytes
- map/filter over an integer_range compute the chunk's values in the loop (chunk_map_first,
  chunk_filter_first) instead of making the range's chunk first
- jank_init's default initial heap 128 -> 256 MiB (env still wins)

A two-capture closure 224 -> 64 bytes, a lazy-seq frame 384 -> 128; count (filter odd? (map inc
(range 1e6))) 61.0 -> 31.0 bytes per element.

Applies on f3d82d65 + 11, 13, 14, 12-21, 18, 19, 15a-16, 15b-17, 22, 23.
